# No environment variables are required to run AniStream, locally or on
# Vercel: every /api/... route the app calls (AniList GraphQL proxy, HiAnime,
# AniKoto, AniVexa, AnimeWixi, ANIME-API, partner analytics, MCP) is served by
# the shared middleware in server/anipmApiHandler.ts — mounted by vite.config.ts
# for `vite dev` / `vite preview`, and by the Vercel serverless catch-all in
# api/[...path].ts for production deployments.
#
# Optional development toggles:
# DISABLE_HMR=true   # disable Vite HMR / file watching (used by AI Studio)
#
# If you later add a third-party API key, keep it here (untracked except for
# this .env.example) and read it through import.meta.env.VITE_* — never hardcode
# keys in src/.
